== v2 REVISION NOTES (this version) ==

This v2 was produced by an independent audit of the Claude consolidated
patch against a separate v1 consolidation. The audit confirmed that the
Claude consolidation made three correct decisions the v1 did not, all in
elf_writer_common.rs (the only file where the two consolidations
differed; all other 26 files were byte-identical):

1. emit_elf relax placement: MOVED OUTSIDE the `if A::supports_deferred_skips()`
   gate. Both concrete X86Arch impls (i686, x86-64) return true, so the
   two placements produce identical output today. But the second
   relax_jumps() call later in emit_elf has always run unconditionally;
   gating only the first call was an inconsistency. The unconditional
   form stays correct if a future arch overrides supports_deferred_skips()
   to false (the first relax pass is about jump encoding, not skip
   deferral, and is a harmless no-op for arches without deferred skips
   since the layout is already final).

2. is_numeric_label check: uses the RESOLVED form (&a_resolved /
   &b_resolved) rather than the raw input (a / b). This handles the
   theoretical case where an ELF-writer alias maps to a numeric label
   string. Unlikely in practice, but strictly more robust.

3. ASCII-digit check: uses num.bytes().all(...) instead of
   num.chars().all(...) for the numeric-label digit check. Equivalent
   for ASCII digits, marginally more efficient (no UTF-8 decode).

Also adopted: Claude's more precise comment on the is_mnemonic check
(".Lfound+1 fails on the '+' before the .L exclusion even applies; the
.L exclusion is what's needed for the bare .Lfound case"), and the
provenance correction noting that Agent B's supplied patch does NOT
contain the directive-vs-macro guard or any resolve_set_expr change
(contradicting Agent A's commit-message narrative about "repairing a
latent bug B's directive guard introduced").

One fix applied to the commit message: test-file count corrected from
"15 files" to "17 files = 15 .c + 2 .flags" (the original miscounted
by excluding the two .flags sidecar files).

No code changes beyond adopting the Claude consolidation's
elf_writer_common.rs. The 26 other files (parser.rs, cli.rs,
vectorize.rs, all encoders, linker, 17 test files) are unchanged from
v1.
